# Input
```css
/* should generate diagnostics */
.a {
	&:is(::before, ::after) {
		content: "";
	}

	.b:not(&::marker) {
		color: red;
	}
}

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.scss:3:7 lint/nursery/noPseudoElementInFunctionalPseudoClass ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × The pseudo-element ::before can't be used inside :is().
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
    2 │ .a {
  > 3 │ 	&:is(::before, ::after) {
      │ 	     ^^^^^^^^
    4 │ 		content: "";
    5 │ 	}
  
  i Pseudo-elements aren't valid inside :is(), :where(), :not() or :has(). Browsers drop the invalid selector, so these styles never apply to the pseudo-element.
  
  i To style the pseudo-element, put it at the end of the selector, outside the pseudo-class, for example .card:is(.featured, .pinned)::before.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

